From 29e601526852d5488754ee2a629ede13c3fe4495 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Claude (sandbox)" <claude@sandbox.local>
Date: Wed, 29 Jul 2026 20:44:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Generic ivr_events ingestion contract: real per-node data
 supersedes the phone-digit/ratio-split guess

The phone-digit route guess and 0.1/0.5/0.4 wait-time split in
twilio_log_ingestion.py aren't bugs -- they're the only thing derivable
from a bare Twilio Call record, which carries no per-node routing data
at all. Real per-node data requires a genuinely different input, and
which real telephony system supplies it (Twilio Studio Flow, TaskRouter,
a custom IVR app's own webhooks) is an integration decision this repo
does not make on Wm's behalf.

Adds a generic contract instead: an optional 'ivr_events' key on the
incoming Twilio record, shaped as a list of {node, wait_seconds, source}.
When present and valid, parse_call_log builds the journey and wait times
directly from it and stamps the result VERIFIED, naming the real source
in the ledger. When absent, nothing changes -- the existing heuristic
runs exactly as before, stamped ESTIMATED. When present but malformed,
parsing fails loud (missing field, negative wait, empty list) rather
than silently degrading to a guess -- a broken real-data integration
should surface as one.

production_harness._assemble_live_episode now reads whichever provenance
twilio_log_ingestion already determined for a given call, instead of
hardcoding ESTIMATED. Caught mid-build: event_v1.validate_event's own
invariant refuses a VERIFIED event that carries a derivation method
(method means DERIVED; verified means observed, not derived) -- the real
source name goes in detail['real_source'] instead, never in method.

DISCLOSED LIMITATION (documented in twilio_log_ingestion's module
docstring): downstream code (SentinelCore.infer_intent, friction
counting, ObservePerceiveCore's resolution detection) still recognizes
queue/agent stops by name convention ('*queue*' substring, literal
agent_a/b/c/d names). A real event source's node names must follow that
same convention for the rest of the pipeline to recognize them --
closing that separate coupling is out of scope here.

Neither twilio_log_ingestion.py nor production_harness.py is in
cassette_forensics._GOVERNANCE_CODE_MODULES, so no cassette code-hash /
version bump is needed for this change.

19 new tests (14 in Tests/test_ivr_events_contract.py covering the
contract at the ingest layer directly, 5 appended to
Tests/test_live_path_kernel_wiring.py covering the VERIFIED path through
the live harness seam). Full suite: 630 passed / 6 skipped (611 baseline
+ 19 new), twice back-to-back from a clean ledger. Ruff clean (0.15.22).
Bandit -ll clean on every touched file.
